    <item>
      <title>Day 1 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-1/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Review &lt;strong&gt;class rules&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;magic questions&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Simple Present&lt;/strong&gt; tense thoroughly.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Learn &lt;strong&gt;regular vs. irregular Simple Past&lt;/strong&gt; verbs.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Focus on &lt;strong&gt;ED ending pronunciation&lt;/strong&gt; and memorize &lt;strong&gt;80 common verbs&lt;/strong&gt; for storytelling and past events.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will reinforce &lt;strong&gt;Week 1 foundations&lt;/strong&gt; while introducing &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past&lt;/strong&gt; verbs. As A1 students, you must follow the class rules and use the &lt;strong&gt;magic questions&lt;/strong&gt; for English-only participation. Finally, you will memorize past tense verbs to describe yesterday&amp;rsquo;s actions or experiences.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 2 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-2/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past with &amp;ldquo;to be&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; (was/were) in affirmative, negative, and question forms.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past with other verbs&lt;/strong&gt; (regular &amp;amp; irregular) for completed actions — affirmative, negative, interrogative, and short answers.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Focus on &lt;strong&gt;pronunciation&lt;/strong&gt; and use past tense for &lt;strong&gt;storytelling&lt;/strong&gt; and past events.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will use the &lt;strong&gt;Simple Past tense&lt;/strong&gt; to talk about finished actions — &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;I went yesterday.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt; As A1 students, use it for recapping weekend plans or sharing life experiences beyond present routines.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 3 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-3/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;possessive adjectives&lt;/strong&gt; to indicate belonging or ownership to a person, animal, or thing.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;possessive pronouns&lt;/strong&gt; to replace a possessive adjective + noun and avoid repetition.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Form a &lt;strong&gt;possessive noun&lt;/strong&gt; by adding &lt;strong&gt;&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/strong&gt; (or &lt;strong&gt;&amp;rsquo;&lt;/strong&gt;) to show ownership.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will use &lt;strong&gt;possessive adjectives&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;pronouns&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;nouns&lt;/strong&gt; to show ownership or a close relationship to someone or something.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 4 - Week 2</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-4/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/Ingles-Material/a1/semana-2/dia-4/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;🎯 Learning Objectives &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At the end of the class, you will be able to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Learn the different &lt;strong&gt;prepositions of time&lt;/strong&gt; and know when to use them.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use the different &lt;strong&gt;prepositions of place&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Use &lt;strong&gt;demonstrative adjectives&lt;/strong&gt; to point and refer to objects.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Learn new vocabulary about &lt;strong&gt;navigating online&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;✅ Describe the way of doing something using &lt;strong&gt;adverbs of manner&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-introduction&#34; class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;📖 Introduction &lt;span class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700&#34; style=&#34;text-decoration-line: none !important;&#34; href=&#34;#-introduction&#34; aria-label=&#34;Ancla&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Today you will learn new vocabulary about &lt;strong&gt;technology&lt;/strong&gt;. At the end of the class, you will know how to use &lt;strong&gt;prepositions of time and place&lt;/strong&gt;. You will also know how to refer to objects that are &lt;strong&gt;near or far&lt;/strong&gt; from you. Finally, you will be able to describe &lt;strong&gt;how something is done&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
